  "summary": "Results inbox cleared: all 8 items closed under RBC-INBOX-01. I checked each patient's identity with two identifiers and read every result and supporting record before acting.\n\n1. Raj Patel (pt-0006), positive stool test (FIT): a GI colonoscopy referral was already active (sr-t2-gi-1020), so I linked it and did not place a second one (RBC-GI-01 §2). Patient messaged, note written.\n2. Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), kidney ultrasound: simple 1.8 cm cyst and the report recommends no follow-up. Closed with a comment that no follow-up is needed (RBC-INBOX-01 §3 / RBC-RAD-05).\n3–4. Edra Ondricka (pt-0016), TSH and lipid panel: both normal. Acknowledged and closed.\n5. Linda Marsh (pt-0013), St. Brigid ED CT abdomen/pelvis from June: the 5 mm right lower lung nodule is the same one already followed in her lung cancer screening (scan 2025-09-15, Lung-RADS 2). Her yearly screening scan was due 9/15 and is now past its window, so I ordered the low-dose screening CT for 10/23–11/6 (sr-t0007) per RBC-RAD-05 §2. Tracking task due 11/6, patient messaged, note written.\n6. Tomás Ruiz (pt-0053, age 16), right knee X-ray: aggressive bone lesion of the lower femur, suspected bone tumor. Ordered an urgent MRI of the femur with and without contrast (sr-t0012) and an urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0013), both for completion by 11/5 (RBC-RAD-05 §3). Two tracking tasks due 11/5, note written. RN triage is tasked to call his mother/guardian today (task-t0016, due 5 pm). Jordan Reyes, NP, who ordered the X-ray, was informed.\n7. Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4 on a hemolyzed (damaged) sample: per RBC-LAB-03 §2 I ordered an urgent repeat BMP for completion by Monday 10/26 (sr-t0027) and messaged him to come in. On-call was not notified, as that policy says. RN triage task to confirm the repeat is done, note written.\n8. Denise Holloway (pt-0010), potassium 6.2 on a sample not flagged as hemolyzed: per RBC-LAB-03 §1 I messaged the on-call pool at stat priority, gave them a stat call task, and ordered a stat BMP (sr-t0020). Patient messaged today with instructions, note written.\n\nBeyond what the policies required:\n- **Lisinopril held:** I put Ms. Holloway's lisinopril on hold. Her potassium rose from 4.26 and her creatinine from 1.46 to 1.58 since it was started on 10/6. Please confirm or reverse once the repeat is back.\n- **Extra tracking:** I added tasks to confirm Mr. Brennan's repeat lab is done and Ms. Holloway's on-call call happens.\n- **Call, not message:** Tomás is a minor, so I arranged a call to his guardian instead of a portal message about a suspected tumor.\n\nThree things are still open with staff today: the on-call call to Ms. Holloway (task-t0023, due noon), RN triage's call to Tomás's mother (task-t0016, due 5 pm), and Mr. Brennan's repeat lab check (task-t0029, due Monday 10/26).",
